### ReWave network — system endpoints and auth examples.
### Variable sources: requests/http-client.env.json (JetBrains) or .vscode/settings.json (VS Code REST Client).

### Liveness probe — live 
# Expected: 200 {"status":"ok"}
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### List channels with an OAuth2 bearer token (pattern for AUTH_MODE=jwks)
# With the local default AUTH_MODE=off the token is ignored; with jwks mode,
# put a real access token into {{token}} (http-client.private.env.json or the
# VS Code settings) — it must carry the scope channels:read.
# Expected: 200 (channel list)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/channels HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List channels without a token while AUTH_MODE=jwks
# Expected: 401 + WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm="rewave-network"
# (not reproducible locally with AUTH_MODE=off — shown for documentation)
# GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/channels

### Unknown channel id — expected: 404
# GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/channels/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000

### Malformed channel id (not a UUID) — expected: 400
# GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/channels/not-a-uuid
